When I initialize parent members, I group the stanza under the heading "Initialize &lt;their base class>":

```c++
// Initialize Control
dwPosX = x;
dwPosY = y;
dwWidth = width;
dwHeight = height;
```

to both inform the reader where the variables are coming from, and also in the future if this happens with multiple parents, you can verify that the most basic parent initialization comes before the least basic.
